      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Sharks have different kinds of teeth. Many have rows of them. The teeth help sharks eat different foods. Check out these shark teeth."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Small, Flat Teeth"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This is a nurse shark (above). Its teeth look almost flat. But its strong jaws can crush food."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Long, Sharp Teeth"
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "url": "https://www.timeforkids.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/K1_260501_long_sharp_teeth.jpg?w=1024",
        "alt": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This is a blue shark. See its pointy teeth? They help this shark chew small fish or squid."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Giant Teeth"
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "url": "https://www.timeforkids.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/K1_260501_giant_teeth.jpg?w=1024",
        "alt": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This great white shark eats big prey. So it has big teeth. They fall out and are replaced."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Big Shark, Small Teeth"
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "url": "https://www.timeforkids.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/K1_260501_big_shark_small_teeth.jpg?w=1024",
        "alt": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This giant whale shark has tiny teeth. They do not bite or chew. These sharks are filter-feeders."
      }
    ]
  },
